---
// ARCHIVED (2026-11-21): the page is noindex, opens with a dated banner and is not linked from the
// navigation. It describes the candidate-ingestion pipeline as designed in April 2026; that pipeline ran once
// and is not in use (REWIEW_NOV_21.md G5, J2, J3).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArchivedBanner from '../components/ArchivedBanner.astro';
import { graph } from '../lib/data.ts';

// Tools whose provenance says they came through this pipeline, counted from data/tools.
const allTools = Object.values(graph.tools);
const viaPipeline = allTools.filter((t) => String(t.provenance?.source ?? '').startsWith('pipeline')).length;

type Step = {
  title: string;
  subtitle?: string;
  detail: string;
  tone?: 'input' | 'staging' | 'process' | 'review' | 'canonical';
};

const steps: Step[] = [
  {
    title: 'Discovery sources',
    subtitle: 'Perplexity Sonar Pro / Elicit / Semantic Scholar / GitHub / awesome-lists',
    detail:
      'Each source is queried on its own cadence with its own rate budget. Perplexity for fresh frontier-agent news, Elicit + S2 for the academic corpus, GitHub for code-level discovery, awesome-lists as a cheap prior.',
    tone: 'input',
  },
  {
    title: 'Postgres: raw_search_results',
    subtitle: 'landing zone, dedup on (source, content_hash)',
    detail:
      'Raw JSON is preserved verbatim for audit. Duplicate rows across re-runs collapse on a deterministic content hash of URL + title. No LLM has touched the data yet at this stage.',
    tone: 'staging',
  },
  {
    title: 'NLP preprocess',
    subtitle: 'keyword match + entity extraction + fuzzy dedup',
    detail:
      'Regex-first entity extraction (github.com/owner/repo, arXiv ids, DOIs). Keyword dictionary maps query terms into SAICA-KG FailureMode ids. Dedupe by canonical URL and by rapidfuzz title similarity ≥ 92.',
    tone: 'process',
  },
  {
    title: 'candidate_tools (pending)',
    subtitle: 'status: pending → reviewed → accepted → graduated',
    detail:
      'One candidate per proposed tool. nlp_tags column carries keyword hits and relevance score; extracted column is empty until the next stage runs.',
    tone: 'staging',
  },
  {
    title: 'Cohere Rerank v4.0 Pro',
    subtitle: 'semantic relevance filter',
    detail:
      'Re-ranks a pool of pending candidates against a SAICA-KG domain query and writes a relevance score to each candidate. It rejects nothing by itself.',
    tone: 'process',
  },
  {
    title: 'Azure Kimi-K2.5 extraction',
    subtitle: 'structured output via OpenAI-compatible client',
    detail:
      'Pydantic schema pins the output shape: id, name, tagline, description, repository_url, supervised failure modes, control_paradigm, temporal_phase, autonomy_level, evidence quotes, per-field confidence. Responses are cached on (prompt_version, kind, candidate_id, source_url).',
    tone: 'process',
  },
  {
    title: 'Human-review graduation CLI',
    subtitle: 'python -m pipeline.cli.graduate tool <id>',
    detail:
      'Pops an accepted candidate from Postgres, writes a YAML stub into data/ with # REVIEW REQUIRED tags on every low-confidence field, and opens it for manual completion. The design asked for a human to review every field before a commit. In the one real run (April 2026) candidates were approved in batches within seconds, so the fields were not reviewed one by one.',
    tone: 'review',
  },
  {
    title: 'data/tools/*.yml (canonical)',
    subtitle: 'Git-diffable, PR-reviewable, CI-validated',
    detail:
      'Canonical YAML is the only thing the paper cites and the website renders. Postgres is staging, not the source of truth. validator/cli.py enforces cross-node invariants on every PR.',
    tone: 'canonical',
  },
];

const TONE_BORDERS: Record<NonNullable<Step['tone']>, string> = {
  input: 'border-l-4 border-l-sky-500',
  staging: 'border-l-4 border-l-amber-500',
  process: 'border-l-4 border-l-violet-500',
  review: 'border-l-4 border-l-rose-500',
  canonical: 'border-l-4 border-l-emerald-600',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  noindex
  title="Ingestion pipeline (archived, April 2026)"
  description="Archived design note from April 2026: how supervision tools were meant to enter SAICA-KG through discovery, staging, extraction and review. The pipeline is not in use."
>
  <h1>Ingestion pipeline</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 mb-6 text-lg text-ink-muted max-w-3xl">
    How a supervision tool was meant to go from a noisy search result to a canonical YAML
    node in <code>data/tools/</code>.
  </p>

  <ArchivedBanner label="Archived design note, not maintained" asOf="23 April 2026">
    <p>
      This page describes the candidate-ingestion pipeline as it was designed in April 2026. The pipeline ran
      for one night and has been dormant since 23 April 2026: {viaPipeline} of the {allTools.length} tools in the
      catalog came through it. The catalog is now kept directly in the YAML files under <code>data/</code>,
      without this pipeline. Read the steps below as a design record, not as how the catalog is maintained today.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Three statements of the original page did not match the code or what happened, and are corrected below
      (project review, 21 November 2026). Tool files were drafted by an LLM or an agent and then edited; fields
      were not reviewed one by one, and in the one real run candidates were approved in batches within seconds.
      The review threshold in the code is 0.85, not 0.7. The reranker only writes a score; it rejects nothing.
    </p>
  </ArchivedBanner>

  <section class="mt-6 max-w-3xl leading-7">
    <p>
      The canonical source of truth is YAML under <code>data/</code>. Postgres is
      staging only &mdash; it is not served to end-users and is not cited by the
      paper. The editorial-governance story (PRs, maintainer review, stability
      commitments) stays intact while automation handles the noise upstream.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      <strong>The design asked for human review before every commit.</strong> Fields
      with confidence below 0.85 were to be tagged <code># REVIEW REQUIRED</code> in the
      YAML stub for a person to fill in. In the one real run this did not hold:
      candidates were approved in batches within seconds, so fields were not
      reviewed one by one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
    <ol class="space-y-2" aria-label="Pipeline steps">
      {steps.map((step, i) => (
        <>
          <li class={`card ${TONE_BORDERS[step.tone ?? 'process']}`}>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
              <div class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">
                Step {i + 1}
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-1 font-sans font-semibold">{step.title}</div>
            {step.subtitle && (
              <div class="mt-0.5 text-sm text-ink-muted"><code>{step.subtitle}</code></div>
            )}
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6">{step.detail}</p>
          </li>
          {i < steps.length - 1 && (
            <li aria-hidden="true" class="flex justify-center py-1">
              <span class="font-sans text-ink-faint">&darr;</span>
            </li>
          )}
        </>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl leading-7">
    <h2>What stays out of scope</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 text-sm space-y-1">
      <li>Postgres does NOT serve end-users. The website + JSON API read from YAML.</li>
      <li>Postgres is NOT replicated for v0.1 &mdash; local dev only. Managed DB is a v0.2 deployment concern.</li>
      <li>
        The design asked that no LLM output be committed without human review, with a
        <code>REVIEW REQUIRED</code> marker on low-confidence fields. That did not hold in
        the one real run (see the note at the top).
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl leading-7">
    <h2>Read more</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 text-sm space-y-1">
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA/blob/main/research/PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md" rel="noopener">
          research/PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md
        </a> &mdash; full architecture, Postgres schema, rate-limit table, and extraction constraints.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA/blob/main/research/ARCH_REVIEW_SYSTEM_DESIGN.md" rel="noopener">
          ARCH_REVIEW_SYSTEM_DESIGN.md
        </a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA/blob/main/research/ARCH_REVIEW_RELIABILITY.md" rel="noopener">
          ARCH_REVIEW_RELIABILITY.md
        </a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA/blob/main/research/ARCH_REVIEW_GOVERNANCE.md" rel="noopener">
          ARCH_REVIEW_GOVERNANCE.md
        </a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA/blob/main/EDITORIAL_POLICY.md" rel="noopener">
          EDITORIAL_POLICY.md
        </a> &mdash; scope, inclusion criteria, RFC process.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="mt-10 text-xs text-ink-faint font-sans">
    Diagram as designed in April 2026; it does not describe the current catalog (SAICA-KG v{graph.kgVersion}).
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
